{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791639905,"nonce":"DREjYEnMmI6HlRPeYQMAGKFjeyA=","title":"cn dropdown, select, popover and combobox rebuild themselves on hover, open and every keystroke","message":"Each was a single Stateful\u003cButtonState\u003e over its whole widget:\n\n- dropdown_menu: the trigger, with deps on the open state. Rebuilt to flip the chevron, to call a custom trigger builder with the open flag, and on each hover/press for the Outline fill.\n- select: the whole select, list included, with deps on value and open. Click-outside was registered and unregistered as a side effect of each rebuild.\n- popover: the trigger, with deps on open, to call its builder with the open flag.\n- combobox: the whole combobox with deps on value, open and the search query, so every keystroke rebuilt it, the search text input being typed into included.\n\nFix (one commit each): the fills and borders are computeds over the element's Interaction and the open state; the dropdown chevron turns by a bound rotation; a custom trigger (dropdown, popover) is swapped through show_or for the form its builder makes; select and combobox show their value through a keyed for_each (select) or a bound Text (combobox), build their list with show(open), and register click-outside inside that branch with Owner::on_cleanup removing it; the combobox's rows are a for_each over the rows matching the search (options, or \"no results\" plus the custom-value row), so the search field is built once per opening. cn's use_button_state / reset_button_state, left without callers, are removed.\n\nTests (blinc_cn/tests): dropdown_trigger_in_place, select_in_place, popover_trigger_in_place, combobox_in_place. Every pointer and key step is checked for subtree rebuilds; all fail against the old components. The combobox test lets through rebuilds inside its search field, which is a text_input, still rebuilt on focus by that widget.","files":null}]}